# determinism-repeat-permute — the draft-decide-run graph (two source gates,
# two egress paths). This vector pins SPEC §7.5 determinism two ways a runner
# can check: (1) repeating the same activations against this file MUST yield
# byte-identical per-gate verdicts, master decisions and log traces every
# time (`repeat` in transport.json); (2) running the same activations against
# `permutations/reordered.lg` — the same policy with its declarations
# textually reordered (declarations are order-independent in meaning, SYNTAX
# §3) — MUST yield the same per-gate verdicts, master decisions and log
# trace. Neither gate pipes into the other, so there is no topological
# ambiguity for declaration order to resolve (contrast
# topo-fanout-fanin-declared-order): only true re-evaluation determinism is
# exercised here. A determinism vector carries no expected.json: reordering
# declarations changes the declaration-order-dependent parts of the static
# observation by construction (SPEC §9, Order), so only the dynamic result
# (verdict/master/log) is compared — see conformance/README.md.
actor  bot7
human  alice  role legal
gate   draft   risk low    grant bot7
gate   decide  risk high   grant bot7
reserve automated_decision by legal when risk >= high
cord bot7   -> draft
cord bot7   -> decide
cord draft  -> master
cord decide -> master
